<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Sena dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1070 CE – 1230 CE (approx.) · capital Nabadwip</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Hindu dynasty that replaced the Palas in Bengal, patron of the poet Jayadeva, until Bakhtiyar Khalji's raid on Nadia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Senas came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a> and settled in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samanta-sena">Samantasena</a> was a chief. His grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayasena">Vijayasena</a> took advantage of the decline of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/pala-empire">Pala Empire</a> to seize much of Bengal in the late 11th and early 12th centuries, also defeating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/varman-dynasty-of-bengal">Varman dynasty of Bengal</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Senas promoted orthodox <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmanism">Brahmanical Hinduism</a>, granting land to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmins</a> and reshaping Bengali <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">caste</a> society; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ballal-sena">Ballalasena</a> is credited with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kulinism">Kulinism</a> system of Brahmin rank and wrote works on ritual. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakshman-sena">Lakshmanasena's</a> court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabadwip">Nabadwip</a> hosted the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayadeva">Jayadeva</a>, author of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gita-govinda">Gita Govinda</a>, and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> poets. Their capitals included Nabadwip, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramapura">Vikramapura</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaur">Lakhnauti</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1204 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhtiyar-khalji">Bakhtiyar Khalji</a> raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabadwip">Nabadwip</a>, and the aged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakshman-sena">Lakshmanasena</a> fled east. North-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> became the base of Muslim rule, while the Senas held eastern Bengal from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramapura">Vikramapura</a> until about 1230.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sena-dynasty.jpg" alt="Sena dynasty" width="320" height="296"><figcaption>Image: Map created from DEMIS Mapserver, which are public domain. Koba-chan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Senas.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1070 CE – 1230 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nabadwip</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Vijayasena, Ballalasena, Lakshmanasena</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit, Old Bengali</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a>, <a href="/countries/bangladesh">Bangladesh</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sena Empire, Senas of Bengal</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1150&amp;focus=sena-dynasty" aria-label="Sena dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7038 1314 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sena dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7358 1570L7253 1492"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7253 1492h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7358 1570h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7358 1570h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Nabadwip. <a href="/atlas?year=1150&amp;focus=sena-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
